    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>String with source location information.</para><para>The location information is a file name string (empty means generated code) and a line number. Line numbers are one-origin; the first line of a file is numbered 1, not 0.</para><para><xrefsect id="todo_1_todo000091"><xreftitle>Todo</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>What does it mean to have a non-positive line number? What line number should be used for generated code when the <computeroutput>filename</computeroutput> member is empty? </para></xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>    </detaileddescription>
